<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Resistance Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1981">1981</a>–<a href="/years/1995">1995</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Resistance Army was the armed wing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni">Yoweri Museveni</a>'s National Resistance Movement, which waged a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war, the Bush War, against the governments of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tito-okello">Tito Okello</a> from 1981. Growing from a small band of fighters, it took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampala">Kampala</a> in January 1986 and brought Museveni to power. It then became Uganda's national army and was renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uganda-peoples-defence-force">Uganda People's Defence Force</a> in 1995.</p></div>
